{
"text": "[image: Back in Austin after a productive last week! We had a marathon 18 hour hearing, I passed another 5 bills out of committee, and hosted the Brownsville ISD board and some wonderful students from the Valley! #txlege]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/CrJNvV0ubV7/"
},
{
"text": "[image: Big day in committee as we heard important bills that will positively impact our state! HB4, the Data Privacy and Security Act, protects Texans' data rights, while HB 471 protects the health and safety of our first responders when injured on the job. I look forward to continuing the work to make Texas the best state in the country for business. #txlege]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/CpvebBROpHy/"
},
{
"text": "[image: Congratulations to the Santa Rosa Warriors Basketball Team for their 2nd straight district title! Good luck in the playoffs and keep making District 35 proud! #txlege #santarosaisd #hd35]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/CoiJrTWO3vW/"
},
{
"text": "[image: Cookie season is coming to an end. Please support your local Girl Scouts! Get your cookies before they are gone!🍪 #Girldad #GirlScoutCookies #txlege @girlscouts @gs_gstx @heb @ruizlongoria @madisonleelongoria @camillaleelongoria]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/CpGP_rjusGc/"
},
{
"text": "[image: Earlier this session, I sat down with McAllen Cable News to discuss the ongoing legislative session, the budget process, and my legislative priorities. Since our interview, I was appointed to the Conference Committee--- a key role in which I have the opportunity, alongside my House & Senate colleagues, to decide the final Biennium budget. Thank you MCN for allowing me to share my experience and insight with the community.] State Representative Oscar Longoria Mid Session Interview YouTube Video VVV4WVV5bjNDNlFDUEltdWx2WklnTlJRLkxNOVpmN0VqZHM4",
"href": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LM9Zf7Ejds8"
},
{
"text": "[image: Great end to the week! After 5 committee hearings, 2 bills passed out of the House, and dozens of visitors from the Valley, Friday ended with my first bill passed this session! SB 1514, the companion to my HB 4279, updates the Business Organizations Code to give Texas companies an advantage over those based out of state. On to the Governor! #txlege]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/Crl4R-bOEY4/"
},
{
"text": "[image: He is risen! From my family to yours, Happy Easter! #txlege]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/Cq0ZKhGuc3x/"
},
{
"text": "[image: I had a blast selling Girl Scout cookies with my daughter Madison today. It's always great to spend quality time with her, and it's even better when we're supporting her cookie business. I love watching her develop her business skills, confidence, and communication skills. 🍪❤️ #girlscouts #girldad #txlege @gs_gstx @girlscouts @heb @madisonleelongoria #girlscoutcookies🍪 #thisismyheb]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/Co3l_OPOTDG/"
},
{
"text": "[image: I had a productive day meeting with representatives from Cameron County and Harlingen. We discussed parks, transportation infrastructure, drainage, and other vital issues in our community. I look forward to working on these projects for the residents of House District 35! #txlege #cameroncounty #hd35 #rgv]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/CoYJWUjuo92/"
},
{
"text": "[image: I'm honored to announce that today I was appointed Chair of the Business & Industry Committee, as well as a member of the Public Education and General Investigating Committees! Thank you to Speaker Phelan for these appointments. I can't wait to get to work for House District 35 and the State of Texas. #txlege #HD35 #RGV]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/CoaozbCOnhY/"
},
{
"text": "[image: Incredibly proud to honor Leslie Flores of Santa Rosa High School on the House floor today! Leslie is the back-to-back state women's powerlifting champ! She broke personal records in bench, squat, and deadlift - all on her way to lifting over 1,000 pounds. Keep making us proud! #txlege #santarosa #warriors]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/Crbp896OmTa/"
},
{
"text": "[image: It was a busy week in the lege! We heard 25 bills in Business & Industry, I laid out 7 bills in 4 different committees, and we made it through budget day. #txlege]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/CqySdrOOnu8/"
},
{
"text": "[image: It was an honor to recognize Keily Guzman and her parents on the House Floor today! Keily is La Joya ISD's first powerlifting state champion! On her way to the win, she broke the state record in squat (425 pounds) and total lift (1,005 pounds). Congratulations, Keily! #txlege]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/CsXUsbzu8qk/"
},
{
"text": "[image: It's been a great week with friends from back home for RGV Days at the Capitol! Your elected officials from across the Valley met with legislators and staff to discuss priorities and projects to improve the RGV! #txlege #rgv]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/Co-9y4POaj2/"
},
{
"text": "[image: Oscar Longoria State Representative District 35]",
"href": "https://facebook.com/1522116934784213"
},
{
"text": "[image: Oscar Longoria State Representative District 35]",
"href": "https://www.facebook.com/1522116934784213"
},
{
"text": "[image: Oscar Longoria State Representative]",
"href": "https://oscarlongoria.com/"
},
{
"text": "[image: Passing bills on a Saturday is a great end to a productive week! This week I passed 4 bills out of the House and sent 1 bill to the Governor for signing! I also hosted a class from CCA McAllen here at the Capitol! #txlege]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/Cr6Na3fOw2N/"
},
{
"text": "[image: She did it again! Back to Back State Champion 🏆 Leslie Flores from Santa Rosa HS came in 1st in the 148 weight class to take home her second STATE TITLE. Leslie is coached by Coach Erica Molina. Keep making us proud! #txlege #hd35 #santarosa #warriors]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/Cp5yRhBOCHm/"
},
{
"text": "[image: The work in the Public Education Committee continued today as we heard numerous bills. #txlege]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/CpyQm5uuvnR/"
},
{
"text": "[image: This week I toured the National Butterfly Center. Watch this video to learn about Spike, the center's tortoise, and his incredible story.<br /><br />Today, you can donate to the National Butterfly Center to help in their efforts via Facebook or at nationalbutterflycenter.org.<br /><br />In late March, the resident 17-year-old African Spurred Tortoise, was injured after a fire burned down his home. The Mission Fire Department and a U.S. Customs and Border Protection medic responded to the fire and assisted the center in extinguishing it. He was severely hurt, and they did not know if he was going to make it. He has since then had a remarkable recovery. Due to treatments and COVID-19, the center has lost a significant amount of revenue.] National Butterfly Center Tour YouTube Video VVV4WVV5bjNDNlFDUEltdWx2WklnTlJRLnY1YUROUGhDLS04",
"href": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v5aDNPhC--8"
},
{
"text": "[image: To the most important woman in our lives, Happy Mother's Day! I hope you all have a great day with your loved ones. #txlege]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/CsOWQAZt4kJ/"
},
{
"text": "[image: Today was my first hearing as Chair of the Business & Industry Committee. We heard testimony from state agencies responsible for making Texas a better place for employers and employees. #txlege]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/Cpd2j_iupis/"
},
{
"text": "[image: Today was the first hearing of the Public Education Committee. It was insightful to hear from both TEA and the Texas School Safety Center. Education and student safety are crucial topics. I am looking forward to seeing the positive changes that will come from these discussions. #PublicEducation #TexasSchoolSafety #educationmatters]",
"href": "https://www.instagram.com/p/CpN0tOtukhM/"
},
{
"text": "[image: WHEREAS, National GEAR UP Week is taking place from September 21<br />to 25, 2020, and this occasion provides a welcome opportunity to<br />recognize La Joya High School for its participation in this noteworthy<br />event; and<br /><br />WHEREAS, The Gaining Early Awareness and Readiness for<br />Undergraduate Programs is a federally funded initiative designed to<br />empower youth from low-income and minority backgrounds to succeed in<br />postsecondary education; the project awards six- and seven-year<br />grants to states and local partnerships composed of K-12 schools,<br />institutions of higher learning, education agencies, and community<br />organizations; and<br /><br />WHEREAS, GEAR UP offers a wide range of resources and support<br />services to middle school and high school students, such as tutoring,<br />mentoring, financial education, and scholarships, and it improves<br />access to higher education for individuals from underserved<br />communities; and<br /><br />WHEREAS, Through their vision and leadership, the faculty and<br />staff of La Joya High have helped countless young Texans reach their<br />highest potential in the classroom and beyond, and in so doing, they<br />are contributing immeasurably to the future of the Lone Star State;<br />ow, therefore, be it<br /><br />RESOLVED, That National GEAR UP Week be commemorated and that La<br />Joya High School be commended for its commitment to providing a<br />quality education for all students.] Recognizing National GEAR UP Week 2020 at La Joya High School YouTube Video VVV4WVV5bjNDNlFDUEltdWx2WklnTlJRLm5sdEY1SUFZbU9v",
"href": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nltF5IAYmOo"
},
{
"text": "[image: Yesterday was another productive day in the Business & Industry Committee. We heard several bills, including my HB 2497, which keeps Texas the number one state in the country for businesses! #txlege]",
